{
    "shape": "agreements[]: { label, agreementHash, clauses[] } — clauses[j]: { clauseKey, fillsBytes, fillsHash, leaf, membershipProof }: fillsBytes is the canonical JSON of the designer's fills for that clause, fillsHash = keccak256(fillsBytes), leaf = keccak256(keccak256(clauseKey ‖ fillsHash)), membershipProof is the sorted-pair proof of leaf under agreementHash, and agreementHash is the sorted-pair merkle root over every clause leaf (a one-clause agreement's hash is its leaf). assemblies[]: { label, assemblyHash, entries[], terms|null }. slots[i]: { id, agreementHash, agreementBytes, slotContentHash, leaf, membershipProof, provenance } — agreementBytes is the canonical JSON {\"clauses\":{…},\"slot\":i}, slotContentHash = keccak256(agreementBytes), leaf = keccak256(keccak256(assemblyLeafDomain ‖ agreementHash ‖ slotContentHash)) with assemblyLeafDomain = keccak256(\"figaro-assembly-leaf\"), the assembly tree's own leaf shape (the terms leaf takes it too), membershipProof is the sorted-pair proof of leaf under assemblyHash. terms: { leafKey (keccak256(\"figaro-assembly-terms\")), termsBytes (canonical JSON of assemblyClauses), clauseDataHash, leaf } or null when no assembly-scoped clause is composed. provenance: { leafKey (keccak256(\"figaro-agreement-provenance\")), agreementHash, assemblyHash, clauseData (canonical JSON {\"agreementHash\":\"0x…\",\"assemblyHash\":\"0x…\"}, lowercase hex), clauseDataHash = keccak256(clauseData), leaf = keccak256(keccak256(leafKey ‖ clauseDataHash)) }. assemblyHash is the sorted-pair merkle root over every entry leaf and the terms leaf; a one-leaf tree's root is its leaf.",
